1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:02,370
(Ira Flatow:)This is Science Friday.
I'm Ira Flatow.

2
00:00:02,532 --> 00:00:05,702
(Ira Flatow:)My guest today is responsible
for the discovery of the first

3
00:00:05,869 --> 00:00:08,319
(Ira Flatow:)stable super-heavy element.

4
00:00:08,471 --> 00:00:09,811
(Ira Flatow:)Welcome, Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

5
00:00:09,973 --> 00:00:10,813
(Sheldon:)Thank you.

6
00:00:12,309 --> 00:00:13,379
(Sheldon:)The university made me come here.

7
00:00:13,543 --> 00:00:14,543
(Sheldon:)I didn't want to.

8
00:00:16,546 --> 00:00:18,496
(Sheldon:)Big fan of the show.

9
00:00:19,616 --> 00:00:22,066
(Ira:)So, I understand
that you actually discovered

10
00:00:22,118 --> 00:00:23,568
(Ira:)this element by mistake.

11
00:00:25,789 --> 00:00:27,459
(Sheldon:)Yes.

12
00:00:27,991 --> 00:00:30,491
(Ira:)And some people in the science
community are calling it

13
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:32,500
"The Wonder Blunder."

14
00:00:32,662 --> 00:00:34,162
(Sheldon:)Who?
Give me their names.

15
00:00:34,331 --> 00:00:35,781
(Sheldon:)I bet it's Wolowitz.

16
00:00:36,733 --> 00:00:38,443
(Ira:)It's just such a fascinating story.

17
00:00:38,602 --> 00:00:39,982
(Ira:)Your calculations are way off,

18
00:00:40,136 --> 00:00:42,346
(Ira:)but they find the element anyway.

19
00:00:42,505 --> 00:00:44,675
(Ira:)It's like misreading
a treasure map

20
00:00:44,841 --> 00:00:47,081
(Ira:)and still finding the treasure.

21
00:00:47,243 --> 00:00:49,083
(Sheldon:)Can we talk
about something else?

22
00:00:49,245 --> 00:00:51,485
(Sheldon:)Do you know that I yodel?

23
00:00:54,184 --> 00:00:55,784
Thats interesting,
but this could be taking you

24
00:00:55,919 --> 00:00:58,159
(Ira:)down the path
toward a Nobel Prize.

25
00:00:58,321 --> 00:00:59,531
(Ira:)And in Chemistry, no less.

26
00:00:59,689 --> 00:01:01,689
(Ira:)And wouldn't that be unusual?

27
00:01:01,858 --> 00:01:04,028
(Ira:)Because you're a physicist.

28
00:01:04,194 --> 00:01:06,334
(Sheldon:)Yes, yes, I'd be a physicist
with a Nobel in Chemistry.

29
00:01:06,496 --> 00:01:08,336
(Sheldon:)Everyone laugh at the circus freak.

30
00:01:09,966 --> 00:01:12,346
(Sheldon:)I don't need to sit
here and take this, Flatow.

31
00:01:13,169 --> 00:01:14,709
(Sheldon:)It is because of bullies like you,

32
00:01:14,871 --> 00:01:16,371
(Sheldon:)every day more and more Americans

33
00:01:16,539 --> 00:01:18,539
(Sheldon:)are making the switch to television.

34
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:22,120
I (THEME SONG PLAYS) I

